---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Review methodology"
  description="How we research, score and update our product reviews."
  path="/methodology/"
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900">Review methodology</h1>
    <div class="content-body mt-6">
      <h2>Where our data comes from</h2>
      <p>
        Our primary sources are manufacturer specification sheets, published third-party professional testing, and
        long-term owner feedback gathered from public forums. Product listings on retail sites are used only for
        reference data such as current price and aggregate customer rating, which are always labelled with the date they
        were captured.
      </p>
      <h2>How we score</h2>
      <p>
        Every review is scored against a published rubric: specification verification, real-world capability versus
        marketing claims, long-term ownership factors (warranty, software support, repair cost), and value at the
        current price. The rubric for each category is listed at the top of that category's comparison page.
      </p>
      <h2>Tested vs. research-based</h2>
      <p>
        Pages labelled <strong>Hands-on tested</strong> include measurements and photographs from units we used
        ourselves. Pages labelled <strong>Research-based</strong> are compiled from primary documents and independent
        testing, with sources cited on the page. We never describe research-based conclusions as first-hand experience.
      </p>
      <h2>How content is produced</h2>
      <p>
        Articles are drafted with AI assistance from source material supplied by our editors, then reviewed and
        fact-checked by a human editor before publication. All numbers — specifications, prices and ratings — are
        verified against the original source at review time.
      </p>
      <h2>Updates</h2>
      <p>
        Every page carries a "last updated" date. Prices are refreshed at least every 48 hours through automated data
        feeds and are labelled with the date they were captured. Review scores are revisited when products receive
        major firmware, hardware or price changes.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
